## 2. One-time setup (Phase 0)

1. Scaffold the repo from the templates: `CLAUDE.md` (from `CLAUDE.md.template`), `{{SPEC}}`, `{{PLAN}}`,
   `{{TASKS}}`; fill the placeholders.
2. Depend on the engine (`{{ENGINE_DEP}}`); wire the engine repo as a read/reference additional directory
   (`.claude/settings.local.json`) so its docs + source are reachable.
3. `.gitignore` covers `.env`, environments, caches, `graphify-out/`, and `.claude/skills/`.
4. Create the uv project, pin Python `>=3.12,<3.13` (match the engine), declare deps with `uv add`, commit
   `uv.lock`.
5. **Build the grounding lanes:** index the installed `rag_wright` package as the `engine` lane and your own repo
   as the `project` lane (the engine's `refresh_framework_graph.sh` is the pattern). Ground every `rag_wright.api`
   call against the `engine` lane before writing it.
6. **Link the skills into `.claude/skills/`:** the engine-authored skills from the engine repo and the shared
   generic skills from their source (symlink so each tracks its version; never copy). Load
   **`using-the-rag-wright-engine`** first on any engine work.
7. Remaining Phase 0: the engine seam, config/secrets, any front-end scaffold, observability, and repaying the
   `{{SPEC}}` placeholders.

