## 4. The build workflow

Each phase has a human review gate; do not advance until approved.

- **Phase 1, Plan.** `interview-me`/`idea-refine` → the discovery set → author `{{SPEC}}` → `{{PLAN}}` (read-only
  Plan Mode).
- **Phase 2, Tasks.** `{{TASKS}}`, each task mapped to its requirement + acceptance, with a verify step and files
  (early phases in full; later phases as headlines, expanded when reached).
- **Phase 3, Contracts.** Define the product contracts (API/tool schemas, workflow I/O) before implementation.
- **Phase 4, Contract-first TDD build, per task.** Ground the calls (engine against the `engine` lane) → failing
  test against the contract → implement to green → verify → short ADR + docs → commit after approval. Write each
  capability's eval first (`creating-evals`).
- **Phase 5, Integrate + end to end.** Wire the surfaces + the engine, run the end-to-end scenarios, confirm
  acceptance.

